[metadata]
Name:niche_stack_split_second
Goal:Survive
Turns:1
Difficulty:Hard
Description:It is your first main phase. You are at 20 life and control two untapped Swamps and three untapped Mountains. Your hand is Sudden Spoiling, Gitaxian Probe, Rite of Flame, Desperate Ritual, Seething Song, Manamorphose, Gut Shot, Empty the Warrens and Goblin Bushwhacker. Your library holds only Colossal Dreadmaw. The opponent is at 33 life and controls Spore Frog, a tapped Vampire Nighthawk, a tapped Typhoid Rats, an untapped Forest and an untapped Swamp, with no cards in hand. Reduce the opponent to 0 life this turn.
Rule:authored-niche-stack-split-second | Spore Frog can be sacrificed for its fog in response to anything, and the fog covers the whole turn, so removal or any spell cast first only invites it; split second (CR 702.61a, 702.61b) lets no player cast spells or activate non-mana abilities while Sudden Spoiling is on the stack, so cast first, before the opponent ever has priority, it strips the Frog of its ability until end of turn (and makes it a 0/2). Spoiling still counts for storm (CR 702.40a): seven spells before Empty the Warrens make 16 Goblins; with the kicked Bushwhacker that is 17 2/1 attackers; the 0/2 Frog, the only untapped blocker, stops one: 32 + Gut Shot's 1 = 33
